'''Seth Adham Curry''' (born August 23, 1990) is an American professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Golden State Warriors]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for one year at [[Liberty Flames basketball|Liberty University]] before transferring to [[Duke Blue Devils men's basketball|Duke]]. He is the son of former NBA player [[Dell Curry]] and the younger brother of NBA player [[Stephen Curry]]. He currently ranks seventh in NBA history in career three-point field goal percentage.<ref>{{Cite web|title=NBA & ABA Career Leaders and Records for 3-Pt Field Goal Pct|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/leaders/fg3_pct_career.html|access-date=March 4, 2025|website=Basketball-Reference.com|language=en}}</ref>

