'''Scott Wayne Barnes Jr.''' (born August 1, 2001) is an American professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Toronto Raptors]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). Born in [[West Palm Beach, Florida]], he attended [[Cardinal Newman High School (West Palm Beach, Florida)|Cardinal Newman High School]] in his hometown before transferring to [[NSU University School]] and later [[Montverde Academy]], where he was rated a consensus five-star [[College recruiting|recruit]] and among the top players in the 2020 class by major recruiting services in his senior year. He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Florida State Seminoles men's basketball|Florida State Seminoles]], being named the [[Atlantic Coast Conference Men's Basketball Rookie of the Year|conference rookie of the year]] among other honours in 2021.

Selected with the fourth overall pick by the Raptors in the [[2021 NBA draft]], Barnes was named the [[NBA Rookie of the Year]] in 2022. After a relatively disappointing sophomore season, his underwent a breakout year in 2024, when he received his first [[NBA All-Star Game|All-Star]] selection and the Raptors pivoted to him as their [[franchise player]], trading away their previous stars. As the Raptors returned to competitivity from a [[Tanking|rebuild]], Barnes received his second All-Star selection and his first on an [[All-Defensive team|All-Defensive Team]] in 2026. Barnes is regarded as a uniquely versatile player, capable of playmaking, ball-handling, and many defensive functions, although his jump shot has been an area of criticism.
